 +0.04 to +0.18), about +1.4\u00b0F since 1896.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months. Highs rose in 4 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Williamsport has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Williamsport's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.46 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.12 to +0.79), about +5.9 inches since 1896. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 43.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (70.26 in); the driest, 1930 (27.68 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}